---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { DISCORD_INVITE_URL } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Server Rules · Meridian"
  description="The general rules governing the Meridian Minecraft server: behavior, cheats, interaction, claims, and moderation."
  path="/rules"
>
<main class="doc rulebook">
  <h1>Server Rules</h1>
  <p class="lead"></p>

  <div class="acc">
    <details class="acc-item" open>
      <summary><h2 id="behavior">Behavior</h2></summary>
      <ol>
        <li>Use common sense.</li>
        <li>Follow the <a href="https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/community-standards" rel="noopener">Minecraft Community Standards</a> and the <a href="https://discord.com/guidelines" rel="noopener">Discord Community Guidelines</a>.</li>
        <li>There is zero tolerance for doxxing, threats, or harassment over in-game events.</li>
        <li>Scamming through trust is not allowed.</li>
        <li>Players may not leverage or participate in rule-breaking.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-item">
      <summary><h2 id="cheats">Cheats</h2></summary>
      <ol>
        <li>Cheat clients, x-ray, dupes, and exploits are prohibited.</li>
        <li>Do not intentionally exploit server bugs.</li>
        <li>Do not intentionally lag, crash, or otherwise disrupt the server.</li>
        <li>Mods that do not provide a significant combat advantage, or information you otherwise could not obtain, are allowed.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-item">
      <summary><h2 id="interaction">Interaction</h2></summary>
      <ol>
        <li>PvP in the wilderness is unrestricted (potions, Mace PvP, etc.).</li>
        <li>Spawn killing or camping a land's spawn is not allowed.</li>
        <li>Griefing is allowed, but land owners may request rollbacks if it obstructs their claim.</li>
        <li>Player traps of any kind are allowed. This does not apply to teleportation traps.</li>
        <li>All farms are allowed, except gold farms.</li>
        <li>Farms that lag the server may be removed by staff.</li>
        <li>Wars are governed separately and require staff approval. See the <a href="/war">Wars</a> section.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-item">
      <summary><h2 id="claims">Claims</h2></summary>
      <ol>
        <li>A land is the property of its owner and trusted members. What happens inside a claim, such as theft or infighting, is for that land's community to handle. This does not apply to rule-breaking.</li>
        <li>Names may not be historical. Inspiration is allowed, but names should be fictitious.</li>
        <li>Claims may not reference extremist ideologies such as Nazism or Stalinism.</li>
        <li>Claims must be reasonably reachable by a normal player on foot or by boat. Claims may not be built entirely underground, entirely floating, or otherwise positioned so that a rival nation could not realistically locate, approach, or lay siege to them.</li>
        <li>Claims that violate these rules may be removed by staff.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-item">
      <summary><h2 id="moderation">Moderation</h2></summary>
      <ol>
        <li>Staff have final say on the enforcement of rules of the server.</li>
        <li>Staff decisions can be appealed via tickets.</li>
        <li>Staff are held to these standards exactly as any other player is.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  <Callout>Questions about a rule, or want to report something? Open a ticket in <a href={DISCORD_INVITE_URL} rel="noopener">our Discord</a>.</Callout>
</main>
</Base>
